{"usCongressBioId":"B001194","familyName":"Butler","givenName":"William","honorificPrefix":"Mr.","unaccentedFamilyName":"Butler","unaccentedGivenName":"William","birthDate":"1759-12-17","birthCirca":false,"birthDateUnknown":false,"deathDate":"1821-11-15","deathCirca":false,"profileText":"a Representative from South Carolina; born in Prince William County, Va., December 17, 1759; attended grammar schools; moved to South Carolina; served in the Revolutionary War during the Snow campaign under General Richardson in 1775 and in Gen. Andrew Williamson's expedition against the Cherokee Indians in 1776; lieutenant in Pulaski's legion, under Gen. Benjamin Lincoln, in 1779; served under Gen. Andrew Pickens at the siege of Augusta in 1780, as captain under General Henderson in 1781, and as captain of Mounted Rangers under General Pickens in 1782; member of the South Carolina state convention which adopted the U.S. Constitution; member of the South Carolina state house of representatives, 1787-1795; sheriff of the Ninety-sixth District in 1791; elected major general of the upper division of South Carolina state militia in 1796; elected as a Democratic Republican to the Seventh and to the five succeeding Congresses (March 4, 1801-March 3, 1813); was not a candidate for reelection; major general commanding the troops raised for the defense of South Carolina during the War of 1812; retired to his plantation on the Saluda River, near Mount Willing, Edgefield County, S.C., and died there November 15, 1821; interment in the family burial ground at Butler Methodist Church, near Saluda, Edgefield (now Saluda) County, S.C.","relationship":[{"relationshipType":"father","relatedTo":{"usCongressBioId":"B001195","familyName":"Butler","givenName":"William","honorificPrefix":"Mr.","unaccentedFamilyName":"Butler","unaccentedGivenName":"William","birthDate":"1790-02-01","birthCirca":false,"deathDate":"1850-09-25","deathCirca":false}}],"asset":[],"jobPositions":[{"job":{"name":"Representative",